invariant: INV-50
file: sha512_compress_blocks.c
catches: sha2_equiv_test
reason: in each pass of sixteen rounds past the first, the first eight
  rounds take the constants of the last eight and the last eight those of
  the first, so every digest a host object computes under the library's
  own names is wrong. eight_rounds_advancing is proved for any eight
  constants, so its proof holds: which constants each call takes is the
  order of the calls, which rests on bin/sha2_equiv_test, and its first
  case differs from the reference.

--- old
            eight_rounds_advancing(&v, &sha512_round_constants[first], ring, 0);
            eight_rounds_advancing(&v, &sha512_round_constants[first + 8], ring, 8);
--- new
            eight_rounds_advancing(&v, &sha512_round_constants[first + 8], ring, 0);
            eight_rounds_advancing(&v, &sha512_round_constants[first], ring, 8);
